<main>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-badge">Quick Start Guide</div>
      <h1>Private AI Running in <span>15 Minutes</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Install Ollama, pull a model, start chatting. No cloud account, no API key, no data leaving your machine.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="steps">
    <div class="container">

      <!-- STEP 0: PICK YOUR MODEL -->
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-number">0</div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h3>Pick Your Model</h3>
          <p>Choose based on your hardware. If you are unsure, start with <strong>Mistral 7B</strong> — it runs on any modern laptop with 8GB RAM.</p>
          <div class="model-grid">
            <div class="model-card">
              <span class="badge badge-green">8GB RAM</span>
              <h4>Mistral 7B</h4>
              <p>Fast, capable, runs on any modern laptop. Best starting point.</p>
              <code class="pull-cmd">ollama pull mistral</code>
            </div>
            <div class="model-card">
              <span class="badge badge-blue">16GB RAM</span>
              <h4>Llama 3.1 8B</h4>
              <p>Meta's latest small model. Strong reasoning, instruction following.</p>
              <code class="pull-cmd">ollama pull llama3.1</code>
            </div>
            <div class="model-card">
              <span class="badge badge-purple">64GB+ RAM</span>
              <h4>Llama 3.3 70B</h4>
              <p>Production-grade. Matches GPT-4 class on most benchmarks.</p>
              <code class="pull-cmd">ollama pull llama3.3</code>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="callout callout-info">
            <div class="callout-title">Not sure what RAM you have?</div>
            Mac: Apple menu → About This Mac → Memory. Linux: <code>free -h</code>. Windows: Task Manager → Performance → Memory.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 1: INSTALL OLLAMA -->
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-number">1</div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h3>Install Ollama</h3>
          <p>Ollama is a one-command runtime that manages models, handles GPU acceleration, and exposes a local API. Free and open source.</p>

          <div class="tab-group">
            <div class="tab-buttons">
              <button class="tab-btn active" onclick="switchTab(event,'mac')">macOS</button>
              <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(event,'linux')">Linux</button>
              <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(event,'win')">Windows</button>
            </div>

            <div class="tab-content active" id="tab-mac">
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-label">Terminal</div>
                <span class="comment"># Option A — Homebrew (recommended)</span><br>
                <span class="cmd">brew install ollama</span><br><br>
                <span class="comment"># Option B — Direct installer</span><br>
                <span class="cmd">curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh</span>
              </div>
              <div class="callout callout-info">
                <div class="callout-title">Apple Silicon</div>
                Ollama automatically uses the Neural Engine on M1/M2/M3/M4 chips. No extra configuration needed. Expect 30–60 tok/s on M3 Pro with Mistral 7B.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="tab-content" id="tab-linux">
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-label">Terminal</div>
                <span class="cmd">curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh</span><br><br>
                <span class="comment"># Ollama installs as a systemd service and starts automatically</span><br>
                <span class="comment"># Verify it is running:</span><br>
                <span class="cmd">systemctl status ollama</span><br>
                <span class="output">● ollama.service - Ollama Service</span><br>
                <span class="output">     Active: active (running)</span>
              </div>
              <div class="callout callout-info">
                <div class="callout-title">NVIDIA GPU</div>
                If you have an NVIDIA GPU with CUDA 11.3+, Ollama detects it automatically. Run <code>nvidia-smi</code> to confirm your driver version before installing.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="tab-content" id="tab-win">
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-label">PowerShell (run as Administrator)</div>
                <span class="comment"># Download the Windows installer</span><br>
                <span class="cmd">winget install Ollama.Ollama</span><br><br>
                <span class="comment"># Or download manually from:</span><br>
                <span class="comment"># https://ollama.com/download/windows</span>
              </div>
              <div class="callout callout-warning">
                <div class="callout-title">Windows Note</div>
                WSL2 is recommended for production use. Native Windows support is stable but GPU passthrough performs better under WSL2 with the CUDA toolkit installed.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 2: PULL MODEL -->
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-number">2</div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h3>Pull Your Model</h3>
          <p>Models download once and are stored locally. Mistral 7B is 4.1GB. Llama 3.3 70B is 43GB. Downloads are resumable.</p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <div class="code-label">Terminal</div>
            <span class="comment"># Replace 'mistral' with your chosen model from Step 0</span><br>
            <span class="cmd">ollama pull mistral</span><br><br>
            <span class="output">pulling manifest</span><br>
            <span class="output">pulling 8034d0d4f706... 100% ▕████████████████▏ 4.1 GB</span><br>
            <span class="output">verifying sha256 digest</span><br>
            <span class="output">writing manifest</span><br>
            <span class="output">success</span>
          </div>
          <div class="callout callout-success">
            <div class="callout-title">Model is stored locally</div>
            After this step, the model never contacts the internet again. All inference is 100% local.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 3: RUN -->
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-number">3</div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h3>Start Chatting</h3>
          <p>Run the model interactively in your terminal, or start the API server for integration with other tools.</p>

          <div class="tab-group">
            <div class="tab-buttons">
              <button class="tab-btn active" onclick="switchTab(event,'cli')">Terminal Chat</button>
              <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(event,'api')">API Server</button>
              <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(event,'ui')">Web UI</button>
            </div>

            <div class="tab-content active" id="tab-cli">
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-label">Terminal</div>
                <span class="cmd">ollama run mistral</span><br><br>
                <span class="output">&gt;&gt;&gt; Send a message (/? for help)</span><br><br>
                <span class="comment"># Type your prompt and press Enter</span><br>
                <span class="cmd">&gt;&gt;&gt; Summarise this NDA in three bullet points: [paste text]</span><br><br>
                <span class="output">• Party A agrees not to disclose...</span><br>
                <span class="output">• Confidentiality period: 3 years...</span><br>
                <span class="output">• Governing law: Delaware...</span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="tab-content" id="tab-api">
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-label">Terminal — start server (runs automatically after install)</div>
                <span class="cmd">ollama serve</span><br><br>
                <span class="comment"># In a second terminal, call the API:</span><br>
                <span class="cmd">curl http://localhost:11434/api/generate \</span><br>
                <span class="cmd">  -d '{"model":"mistral","prompt":"Summarise this contract...","stream":false}'</span><br><br>
                <span class="output">{"response":"The contract establishes...","done":true}</span>
              </div>
              <div class="callout callout-info">
                <div class="callout-title">OpenAI-compatible endpoint</div>
                Ollama also exposes <code>http://localhost:11434/v1/chat/completions</code> — drop-in compatible with any OpenAI SDK. Change the base URL, keep your existing code.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="tab-content" id="tab-ui">
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-label">Terminal — Open WebUI (ChatGPT-style interface)</div>
                <span class="cmd">docker run -d \</span><br>
                <span class="cmd">  -p 3000:8080 \</span><br>
                <span class="cmd">  --add-host=host.docker.internal:host-gateway \</span><br>
                <span class="cmd">  -v open-webui:/app/backend/data \</span><br>
                <span class="cmd">  ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui:main</span><br><br>
                <span class="output"># Then open: http://localhost:3000</span>
              </div>
              <div class="callout callout-info">
                <div class="callout-title">No Docker?</div>
                Install Docker Desktop from <a href="https://docker.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">docker.com</a> — free for personal and small business use. Takes 2 minutes.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 4: VERIFY PRIVATE -->
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-number">4</div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h3>Verify Nothing Left Your Machine</h3>
          <p>Confirm there is no outbound traffic during inference.</p>
          <div class="tab-group">
            <div class="tab-buttons">
              <button class="tab-btn active" onclick="switchTab(event,'v-mac')">macOS</button>
              <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab(event,'v-linux')">Linux</button>
            </div>
            <div class="tab-content active" id="tab-v-mac">
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-label">Terminal — monitor network while running a prompt</div>
                <span class="cmd">sudo lsof -i -n -P | grep ollama</span><br><br>
                <span class="output">ollama  1234  user  TCP 127.0.0.1:11434 (LISTEN)</span><br><br>
                <span class="comment"># 127.0.0.1 = loopback only. No external connections.</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="tab-content" id="tab-v-linux">
              <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-label">Terminal</div>
                <span class="cmd">ss -tulpn | grep ollama</span><br><br>
                <span class="output">tcp LISTEN 0 128 127.0.0.1:11434 users:(("ollama",pid=...))</span><br><br>
                <span class="comment"># Bound to loopback. Zero external traffic.</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="callout callout-success">
            <div class="callout-title">You are fully private</div>
            Ollama only listens on localhost by default. Your prompts, documents, and responses never leave the machine.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- WHAT'S NEXT -->
      <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem; font-weight:700; color:#f8fafc; margin: 48px 0 8px;">What's Next</h2>
      <p style="color:#64748b; margin-bottom:24px;">You have a working private AI. Here is where to go from here.</p>
      <div class="next-grid">
        <a href="/mistral-large/" class="next-card">
          <div class="next-label">Model Guide</div>
          <h4>Mistral Large 2</h4>
          <p>Best-in-class for legal and finance work. 128k context.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/llama/" class="next-card"> <!-- STUB: /llama/ -->
          <div class="next-label">Model Guide</div>
          <h4>Llama 3.3 70B</h4>
          <p>Production-grade open model. GPT-4 class performance.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/compare/vs-chatgpt/" class="next-card">
          <div class="next-label">Comparison</div>
          <h4>vs ChatGPT</h4>
          <p>Why local beats cloud for sensitive work.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="#" class="next-card"> <!-- STUB: /solutions/ -->
          <div class="next-label">Use Cases</div>
          <h4>Solutions</h4>
          <p>Legal, Finance, HR, Dev — right model for each team.</p>
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</main>

